### Landing-design invariants (CI-enforced)

The four mechanically-checkable anti-patterns from
`docs/LANDING_STAGING_PROD_DESIGN.md` are enforced by
`scripts/check_landing_design_invariants.py`, wired into the
`landing-invariants` job in `.github/workflows/agent-enforcement.yml`. Any
PR that introduces one of these fails CI:

1. **Per-department dbt model filenames** — `silver.neris_san_bernardino_*`
   is wrong; `silver.neris_incidents` is right. Universal schema, sparse
   population.
2. **Per-department Gold subdirectories** — `dbt/models/gold/<dept>/` is
   forbidden. Gold is one schema, one row per (department_id, ...key...).
3. **Hardcoded `_department_id` literals** — `WHERE _department_id =
   'portland'` defeats RLS. Use `{{ var('app_department_id') }}` or the
   on-run-start macro from migration 050.
4. **Schema without fixture** — every `schemas/*.yaml` must have a matching
   `tests/fixtures/<source>/*.json`. A schema without a fixture is an
   untestable contract.

The script runs ~50 files in under a second. Local dev: `python3
scripts/check_landing_design_invariants.py`. The four prose-only
anti-patterns (department adapter, raw-payload discarding, branching on
`_department_id`, transform-tool-owns-raw) still require human review at
code-review time.

